================================================================================
LIVE VERIFICATION — 2026-10-26 (harness: tmp-verify-premium.ts, gitignored)
================================================================================
Command (local API on :3000 restarted with connection_limit=5; harness with connection_limit=3,
because the shared Supabase session pool (15) was exhausted by the API + production):
  npx tsx tmp-verify-premium.ts *> tmp-verify-premium.out

Run history (disclosed, harness-side problems, not product failures):
  run 1 — the 3 "session N" checks read `dailyQuestions` at the top level of the response,
          but POST /api/sessions returns { session: { ..., dailyQuestions } }. The served
          counts were already correct (9, 9, 2, then 403). It then crashed with
          EMAXCONNSESSION because the harness opened a second PrismaClient for the
          in-process simulation builder. Left 3 fixture users behind.
  run 2 — the leftover sweep removed run 1's fixtures (fresh query: users=0 resources=0),
          then registration hit the in-memory RATE_LIMITED limiter (429) after 2 users.
          The API was restarted to reset the limiter.
  run 3 — below, verbatim. Its leftover sweep removed run 2's 2 users first.
Fixes between runs: read session.dailyQuestions; share src/lib/prisma's client; add a
leftover sweep (email prefix verify-premium-…@example.invalid, resource sourceLabel VERIFY-PREMIUM…).

Simulation exemption is exercised in-process (buildSessionForUser with enforceDailyLimit:false,
the exact flag POST /api/simulations/:id/start passes) rather than through a real simulation,
so no VERIFY simulation row was ever visible to real students.

Console note: "┬À" below is the middle dot "·" rendered through codepage 850 by PowerShell
redirection — not a data problem (see AGENTS.md encoding note).

